doc The null pointer: a pointer to nothing, compatible with every pointer type.
  ```
  struct Node
    value: int
    next: ptr Node
  end

  let n = new Node
  if n.next == null
    print "last node"
  end
  ```

  Reading a field through `null` crashes the program. A variable declared
  as `let p = null` has no pointee type, so give it one:
  `let p: ptr Node = null`.

syntax expr
  null -> ptr ?
